{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b2511a9f-fbc6-4230-9b85-a48c9ec2356a","step":{"id":"s1","script":"These triangles have the same angles, so they are similar. Their sizes differ, but their shapes match.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Similar triangles: same shape"},{"op":"figure","id":"triangles","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-0.7,10],"y":[-1,6]},"marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"a","at":[0,0],"label":"A"},{"kind":"point","id":"b","at":[3,0],"label":"B"},{"kind":"point","id":"c","at":[0,4],"label":"C"},{"kind":"polyline","points":[{"at":"a"},{"at":"b"},{"at":"c"}],"closed":true},{"kind":"point","id":"d","at":[4.5,0],"label":"D"},{"kind":"point","id":"e","at":[9,0],"label":"E"},{"kind":"point","id":"f","at":[4.5,6],"label":"F"},{"kind":"polyline","points":[{"at":"d"},{"at":"e"},{"at":"f"}],"closed":true},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"a"},"from":{"at":"b"},"to":{"at":"c"}},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"d"},"from":{"at":"e"},"to":{"at":"f"}}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b2511a9f-fbc6-4230-9b85-a48c9ec2356a","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Match corresponding vertices: A with D, B with E, and C with F. The matching bases show a scale factor of one point five.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"bases","on":"triangles","marks":[{"kind":"measure","from":{"at":"a"},"to":{"at":"b"},"label":"3"},{"kind":"measure","from":{"at":"d"},"to":{"at":"e"},"label":"4.5"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"similar","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\triangle ABC\\sim\\triangle DEF"},{"op":"equation","id":"scale","anchor":{"el":"similar","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"k=\\frac{DE}{AB}=\\frac{4.5}{3}=1.5"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b2511a9f-fbc6-4230-9b85-a48c9ec2356a","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Every corresponding side uses that same multiplier. A side of four becomes six. What does a side of five become?","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"lengths","on":"triangles","marks":[{"kind":"measure","from":{"at":"a"},"to":{"at":"c"},"label":"4"},{"kind":"measure","from":{"at":"d"},"to":{"at":"f"},"label":"6"},{"kind":"text","at":[1.9,2.3],"text":"5"},{"kind":"text","id":"unknown","at":[7.2,3.3],"text":"?"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"ratios","anchor":{"el":"scale","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\frac{DE}{AB}=\\frac{DF}{AC}=\\frac{EF}{BC}=1.5"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"If BC = 5, what is EF?","expected_gist":"EF = 5 × 1.5 = 7.5, using the same scale factor."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b2511a9f-fbc6-4230-9b85-a48c9ec2356a","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Five times one point five is seven point five. Similarity means corresponding sides are proportional, not necessarily equal.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"answer_mark","on":"triangles","marks":[{"kind":"text","at":[8,3.7],"text":"7.5"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"answer","anchor":{"el":"ratios","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"EF=1.5\\times BC=1.5\\times5=7.5"}],"checkpoint":null}}
